## ── Component 2: Model weight files ONLY (keep config/tokenizer JSONs) ──
##    Both trees: ignore the heavy weight files, keep the small configs.
##
##    checkpoint/ directories: ignore the heavy weight files only.
component2_entity_relation_extraction/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.safetensors
component2_entity_relation_extraction/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.pt
component2_entity_relation_extraction/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.zip
component2_entity_relation_extraction/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.hdf5
component2_entity_relation_extraction/scripts/checkpoints/**/training_args.bin
component2_entity_relation_extraction/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.bin
com2_using_3models/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.safetensors
com2_using_3models/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.pt
com2_using_3models/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.zip
com2_using_3models/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.hdf5
com2_using_3models/scripts/checkpoints/**/training_args.bin
com2_using_3models/scripts/checkpoints/**/*.bin
##
##    Global fallbacks (catches any other .safetensors/.pt/.zip in repo):
**/*.safetensors
**/*.pt
**/*.zip
**/*.hdf5
**/training_args.bin
**/*.bin
##
##    Files RETAINED (small configs, tokenizer files, F1 eval results):
##      config.json, tokenizer.json, tokenizer_config.json (HF model configs)
##      labels.json (relation label schema)
##      scierc_test_f1.json (NER eval results, ~small)
##      scierc_relation_test_f1.json (relation eval results, ~small)
##      scierc_data/processed_data/json/*.json (train/dev/test splits)

## ── Component 5: Regenerable outputs ────────────────────────────────────

# Structural embeddings (.npy) — regenerable via 02_structural_embeddings.py
**/component5/output/embeddings/structural/*.npy

# Semantic embeddings (.npy) — regenerable via 03_semantic_embeddings.py
**/component5/output/embeddings/semantic/*.npy

# Graph slices (.gpickle) — regenerable via 01_build_slices.py
**/component5/output/slices/*.gpickle

# Full gap sweep (hundreds of alpha-variant files) — regenerable via 04
**/component5/output/gaps/*.json
**/component5/output/gaps/*.meta.json
!**/component5/output/top_gaps_NLP_latest.json
!**/component5/output/top_gaps_COVID_latest.json
!**/component5/output/ablation_NLP.json
!**/component5/output/ablation_NLP.md
!**/component5/output/ablation_COVID.json
!**/component5/output/ablation_COVID.md
!**/component5/output/slices_build_log.json

## ── Component 6: Regenerable outputs ────────────────────────────────────

# Citation caches — regenerable via 01_fetch_citations.py
**/component6/output/citations/*.json
!**/component6/output/citations/COVID_FALLBACK.txt
!**/component6/output/citations/NLP_FALLBACK.txt

# Full rerank sweep (hundreds of alpha-variant files) — regenerable via 03
**/component6/output/reranked/
!**/component6/output/top_velocity_gaps_NLP_latest.json
!**/component6/output/top_velocity_gaps_COVID_latest.json
!**/component6/output/ablation_velocity_NLP.json
!**/component6/output/ablation_velocity_NLP.md
!**/component6/output/ablation_velocity_COVID.json
!**/component6/output/ablation_velocity_COVID.md

## ── Component 2: Intermediate slice/extracted files in alternate tree ───
##    _extracted_slice.json files are scratch intermediates used only by
##    com2_using_3models/scripts/ scripts. _extracted.json files (no _slice)
##    are READ by Components 3, 5, 6 — they contain paper text for validation,
##    so they are KEEP (research inputs, not just intermediates).
**/com2_using_3models/output/*_extracted_slice.json
**/com2_using_3models/output/scibert/*_extracted_slice.json
**/com2_using_3models/output/roberta/*_extracted_slice.json
**/com2_using_3models/output/pubmedbert/*_extracted_slice.json
**/com2_using_3models/output/NLP_entities_slice.json
**/com2_using_3models/output/COVID_entities_slice.json
**/com2_using_3models/output/NLP_relations_slice.json
**/com2_using_3models/output/COVID_relations_slice.json

